module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.a_worktree_delta_against_one_base_applied_onto_another

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data a_worktree_delta_against_one_base_applied_onto_another: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "a_worktree_delta_against_one_base_applied_onto_another" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "**a change set computed against one base is applied onto a different base's tree, and the result is recorded as the worker's candidate** (THE INVALID STATE: gunbc.roadmap_belt_actuate belt_scm_delta_capture took the worktree's change population from `git diff <attempt base_sha>` plus untracked files, and re-bound exactly those paths on the project repository's BASE MANIFEST -- the tree the repository was seeded from. Nothing compared the attempt's base with the repository's. When an attempt branched from a later base than the seed, every upstream path the worker did not touch kept the SEED's bytes, so the recorded candidate was neither the attempt's base plus the work nor any tree that ever existed.)",

    "HARM: silent. The capture minted, the commit carried a plausible message, verification ran against the git edge (which held the REAL tree), and integration merged the SCM candidate -- so the verified tree and the integrated tree were different trees under one name. RECEIPT (srv2, audited 2026-10-03): project shell-typed-invocation was seeded at d012e00; candidates 1, 3 and 4 were captured from attempts on b7f9070, d7005ab and d7005ab. Candidate 1 was integrated as commit 2 (through a capture record naming ordinal 1 with no root locator, accepted by a belt that predated the binding check), so the integration head carried a tree with 26 upstream paths at risk of the wrong bytes. Nothing was published from it only because the publish step had not run.",

    "DISTINGUISHING FACTS: the two bases are each recorded -- the attempt's in its spawn-destination.json base_sha, the repository's in its root commit -- so the defect is a missing JOIN of two recorded facts, not a missing fact. A delta is meaningful only relative to the base it was computed against; applying it elsewhere is the stale-base condition docs/plans/scm-demo-cli-rebuild.md already names ('a moved target is a named stale-base condition, never permission to apply an old stage to a different base'), unmodeled at the belt.",

    "RUNG FOUND AT: below the floor (silent wrongness). RAISED TO 1 by gunbc#13111: the capture refuses typed when the attempt's base_sha is not the base the repository's base commit records, the integrate refuses (durably, as an integration-blocked receipt) a capture recorded from an attempt on another base, and the publish refuses when the integration worktree's base is not the recorded one. The base is still recorded in the root commit's MESSAGE, an untyped carrier compared by string.",

    "CEILING: 4 (structurally impossible) for the capture: a candidate whose ancestry names a base commit carrying a TYPED base record cannot be minted against a different base if the mint consumes the attempt's base as that record. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER: the typed base record and the BaseAdvance transition (the stacked follow-up to this PR): every base commit carries its intake sha as a typed member, candidates descend from the base commit recording their attempt's base, and an advance of the intake base is a commit re-binding exactly git diff old..new -- after which 'which base did this candidate's delta assume' is the candidate's parent, not a string comparison.",

    "RAISED AGAIN by the BaseAdvance follow-up (that trigger, landed): a commit carries a typed intake member (gunbc.scm.intake CommitIntake, envelope format v9), the base and every advance of it are minted by gunbc.scm.repository_envelope mint_intake_base and mint_intake_advance, and the belt's capture finds the intake commit whose revision IS its attempt's base (gunbc.roadmap_belt_actuate belt_scm_intake_base_for), advancing the intake line to it over exactly git diff S_k..S_k+1 when the repository has not met it (belt_scm_base_advance, which refuses an unobservable revision by name). So on the belt route the delta computed against base_sha is applied onto the manifest of the commit recording base_sha, by construction, and the message comparisons are deleted. AT THE SCM INTERFACE the advance's continuity is an admission (rung 3): an advance whose parent's line is not at its `from`, a second advance from one revision, and a second placement of one revision each refuse. REPOSITORIES THAT PREDATE IT (every commit IntakeUnrecordedByFormat) take no new capture and carry typed standings derived on read -- CaptureBaseStale for a candidate captured against another base, IntegratesStale for a commit whose line integrated one (rung 1). WHAT IS NOT YET STRUCTURAL, stated: the candidate mint (gunbc.scm.write_spine commit_staged) takes no revision, so the pairing of 'the delta was computed against base_sha' with 'the parent is the intake commit for base_sha' is held by one belt function, not by a sealed carrier. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER: a capture mint that takes the IntakeRevision its delta was computed against and admits it only when the parent's line stands there, so no route can pair a delta with another base's tree.",

    "THE CORRECTIVE HALF, AFTER THE NO-LAND RULING ON gunbc#13402 (the class's second face: a correction that marks an UNCORRECTED tree clean). Measured: the first supersession admitted any fresh source and merged it INTO the stale integration, so with an upstream-added, worker-deleted path (absent at the stale base, so the worker's deletion had vanished from the stale delta) an unrelated fresh commit 'corrected' the line without conflict and the stale integration left standing with the path present. Now: a commit records the unit of work it captured (gunbc.scm.intake CommitWork); a supersession is admitted only for the exact stale integration X, from a fresh capture of the SAME work, once; and the corrective commit is X's child whose root is the recapture merged into X's PARENT (gunbc.scm.repository_envelope admit_supersession), so X's wrong delta is discarded rather than merged over. THE DECODER RE-RUNS ALL OF IT (supersession_census, with the corrected-root equality on a whole store; gunbc.scm.repository_load indexed_supersession_roots reads exactly the manifests an indexed load needs) together with the intake laws (intake_census: one base, a root; advances continue their parent's line; a revision placed once and left by one advance; no half-converted population; stale captures off their line's base and naming their work) -- so edited bytes cannot assert a correction or an intake history the mints would refuse. A repository holds ONE intake line (a second base refuses; tip and revision lookups answer typed ambiguity, never list order). Witnessed: test.claim.roadmap.roadmap_belt_supersession_witness_test (the corrected manifest, the unrelated-source red) and test.claim.scm.scm_intake_census_witness_test (six forged-v9 reds, two positive controls). THE SECOND NO-LAND RULING closed the label itself: the work identity is a record of two members (gunbc.scm.intake CaptureWork { unit, attempt }), compared field by field, so the delimiter collision (n, 'x ay') vs ('n ax', y) that the first, rendered spelling admitted is two identities (test.claim.scm.scm_intake_census_witness_test a_delimiter_collision_is_two_identities; restoring the rendered equality turns it red); and work is read only through an admitted capture (gunbc.scm.repository_envelope admit_capture: non-root, integrated nothing, intake none or stale), which the census applies to every row carrying work, so the recaptured work's identity attached to an intake base, an advance, an integration or a correction refuses on decode. STILL HELD BY DILIGENCE: a correction is admitted only while X is the head, so a stale integration with later integrations on top needs a replay the model does not yet carry (refused, typed, at the belt entry).",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
